// here an era tag and an approximate date tag are given.
//
// Sources consulted (research pass, Oct 2026):
//   Mokyr, The Lever of Riches — TOC (2 Classical antiquity; 3 The Middle Ages; 4 The Renaissance and
//     beyond 1500–1750; 5 The years of miracles: the Industrial Revolution 1750–1830; 6 The later
//     nineteenth century 1830–1914; 7 Understanding technological progress):
//     https://www.fulcrum.org/concern/monographs/m900nt69d
//   Usher, A History of Mechanical Inventions — chapter titles verified (Water wheels and windmills
//     150 B.C.–A.D. 1500; Water clocks and mechanical clocks; The invention of printing; Clocks and
//     watches as instruments of precision 1500–1800; Machine tools and quantity production; textile
//     machinery; power production), numbers not: https://biblioteca.juaneloturriano.com/Record/Xebook1-2393
//   Cardwell, Wheels, Clocks, and Rockets — partial TOC only (Clockwork and Christianity; The
//     Industrial Revolution; Power without wheels); cited at book level:
//     https://preview.wellcomecollection.org/works/ak6vec5s
//   Courses: MIT STS.007 Technology in History; STS.340J Introduction to the History of Technology;
//     STS.460 Histories of information, communication and computing:
//     https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/sts-340j-introduction-to-the-history-of-technology-fall-2006/pages/syllabus/
//   Lists: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_historic_inventions (stone tools, fire, pottery,
//     wheel, smelting, Archimedes' screw, water wheel, astrolabe, paper, compass, stirrup, horse
//     collar, crank and connecting rod).
// Gaps filled after comparison: bow and spear-thrower, paper, crank and connecting rod, stirrup,
//   heavy plough and horse collar, windmill, canal pound lock, barometer and vacuum pump (needed by
//   the steam engine and the light bulb), boring mill and interchangeable parts, Bessemer steel,
//   Jacquard loom (punched cards → computing), steam turbine, vaccination and germ theory, synthetic
//   dyes, refrigeration, jet engine and rocket, quartz and atomic clocks, optical fibre,
//   public-key cryptography, lithium-ion battery, solar cell, PCR.
// Deliberate omissions: agricultural machinery beyond the plough, military history beyond
//   gunpowder and the gun, nuclear weapons, software history beyond the stored program and the web.
